{"content":[{"c":["MEREMOTH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Priest, son of Uriah, grandson of Hakkoz (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.33","r":"Ezra.8.33","rawR":"Ezra.8.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.33","value":"Ezra.8.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.4,21","r":"Neh.3.4,21","rawR":"Neh.3.4,21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.4,21","value":"Neh.3.4,21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:4, 21"},"). The family of Hakkoz was unable to prove its descent; therefore, they were excluded from the priesthood. Meremoth appears to be an exception. He weighed silver and gold (a priestly function [",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.24-30","r":"Ezra.8.24-30","rawR":"Ezra.8.24-30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.24-30","value":"Ezra.8.24-30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:24-30"},"]), repaired part of the Jerusalem wall (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.4,21","r":"Neh.3.4,21","rawR":"Neh.3.4,21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.4,21","value":"Neh.3.4,21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:4, 21"},"), and sealed the covenant (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.5","r":"Neh.10.5","rawR":"Neh.10.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.5","value":"Neh.10.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:5"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Priest and Bani’s son, who severed ties with his foreign wife and children at Ezra’s request (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.36","r":"Ezra.10.36","rawR":"Ezra.10.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.36","value":"Ezra.10.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:36"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Priest who returned from Babylon with Zerubbabel (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.3","r":"Neh.12.3","rawR":"Neh.12.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.3","value":"Neh.12.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:3"},") and established the house of priests called Meraioth in ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.15","r":"Neh.12.15","rawR":"Neh.12.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.15","value":"Neh.12.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nehemiah 12:15"}," (though some identify the two references as the same person)."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Meremoth","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ezr 8:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.8.33","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.8.33","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.8.33"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:4, 21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.4,21","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.4,21","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.4,21"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 8:24-30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.8.24-30","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.8.24-30","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.8.24-30"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:4, 21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.4,21","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.4,21","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.4,21"},{"anchorText":"10:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.10.5","rawQueryValue":"Neh.10.5","sourceRefExact":"Neh.10.5"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:36","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.36","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.36","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.36"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.3","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.3","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.3"},{"anchorText":"Nehemiah 12:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.15","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.15","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.15"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"7de6b6d15f3d2fcc72f2a98bbdc9ccfbcc63c5615465a2d96f944d00b22a9b53","sourceItemName":"Meremoth","sourceItemOrder":259,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Meremoth","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Meremoth","title":"Meremoth","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}